  "details": "In the Unity 2022 Open Beta, the volume sliders have no influence on the reverb effects produced by Reverb Zones.\n\nTo test, use this world called 'Audio Demo': \n\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_40ba745f-3360-4e50-8e88-aba1b56ffaa3\n\nAfter you spawn, look behind-left for the \"Reverb Zone\" demo area. Use the 'Monster Roar Toggle' button. Open the VRChat settings menu and try muting the World Volume or Master Volume.\n\nIn the Open Beta, the reverb effect of the monster's roar will remain audible even though the dry audio is silenced. In Live, both the dry audio and the reverb effect are silenced.\n\nThe problem also applies to avatar audio. If you have Avatar Volume or Master Volume muted, you'll still be able to hear the reverberations of avatar audio while in a Reverb Zone.",
